\n- [L /_404.html] Course Catalog\n- [L /_404.html] Campus Libraries\n- [L /_404.html] Learning Support Services\n- [L /_404.html] Tech Accessibility\n- [L /_404.html] Discovery\n#### Support Services\n- [L /_404.html] Career Studio\n- [L /_404.html] Technology on Campus\n- [L /_404.html] Office of the Dean\n- [L /_404.html] First-Generation Scholars\n- [L /_404.html] Housing and Meals\n- [L /_404.html] Office of the Student Advocate\n- [L /_404.html] Support for Students with Disabilities\n- [L /_404.html] Student Jobs & Employment\n- [L /_404.html] Student Health & Counseling\n- [L /_404.html] Well-Being Alliance\n#### Campus Employment\n- [L /_404.html] Student Jobs & Employment\n- [L /_404.html] Campus Life Employment\n- [L /_404.html] Graduate Assistant Positions\n#### Academic, Research & Cultural Programs\n- [L /_404.html] Arts\n- [L /_404.html] Innovation & Entrepreneurship\n- [L /_404.html] Global Corravale\n- [L /_404.html] Our Roots\n- [L /_404.html] Green Campus\n[IMG The 3-D Visualization Lab inside the Halverson Center on North Ridge @@ /media/images/sidebar-images/currentstdnt-3dlab.jpg]\nP: The 3-D Visualization Lab at the Merriston Center on North Quadrant\n## Onward Now\n[IMG Block C @@ /includes/panels/gallery/images/block-m-maize.png]\n[IMG 24 Hours @@ /includes/panels/gallery/images/24-hours.png]\n### All Corravale, all the time\nP: There's always something remarkable unfolding at Corravale. Whether it's across our campuses or somewhere far beyond them, our students, faculty, staff and alumni are busy chasing what's next. A selection of moments gathered over the years fills the gallery below.\n- \n[IMG The Aldridge Nature Reserve offers research and teaching opportunities across the natural sciences. @@ /_images/placeholder_500.svg]\n6:42 am\n- \n[IMG A student gets ready for a morning class in the sunlit atrium of the Meridian School of Business. @@ /_images/7d2e5d9e21f26e36.jpg]\n6:17 am\n- \n[IMG Members of the women's tennis team run through an early morning workout at the Calder Field House. @@ /_images/a3bf3e87673f2073.jpg]\n7:33 am\n- \n[IMG A student worker readies the register for a new day at the Corravale Union. @@ /_images/a5cf54c08444dbdc.jpg]\n7:09 am\n- \n[IMG A machinist working in the Corravale Scientific Instrument Shop. @@ /_images/daba8bbd39dfbe1a.jpg]\n8:05 am\n- \n[IMG A research technician working in a laboratory at the Whitfield Cardiovascular Center. @@ /_images/09d25592b3019959.jpg]\n8:48 am\n- \n[IMG Student musicians pound out rhythms on five gallon buckets during the pre-show entertainment at Spring Commencement. @@ /_images/3fa3f186d919642b.jpg]\n9:11 am\n- \n[IMG ROTC cadets work together to hold and unfold a large national flag outside the Chemistry building near the central green flagpole during the annual Veterans Day flag-raising ceremony. In the background, cadets from the various ROTC programs stand at attention. @@ /_images/044d154eb1914a4a.jpg]\n9:37 am\n- \n[IMG Medical students and residents speak with a patient and her mother during morning rounds at the Cranmore Children's Hospital. @@ /_images/65b119af71e6c236.jpg]\n9:53 am\n- \n[IMG A group of seven students in Corravale gear smile and pose for a photo taken by a parent in a blue tee shirt at the Parents and Family Weekend Tailgate event in the Calder Field House. @@ /_images/c342b80512e466ef.jpg]\n9:20 am\n- \n[IMG A research scientist at the Corravale Herbarium sorts seeds from plant specimens collected in the field. @@ /_images/26143309ced199d0.jpg]\n10:34 am\n- \n[IMG A Halverson Center audio resource manager works on three-dimensional sound for digital preservation, academic research and entertainment. @@ /_images/placeholder_500.svg]\n10:07 am\n- \n[IMG A student in a gray hooded sweatshirt with headphones in works on their laptop in front of large windows looking out on the Hartwell Hall spires in the Ellison Undergraduate Library. @@ /_images/placeholder_500.svg]\n10:29 am\n- \n[IMG A worker enters the campus Nanofabrication Facility on North Ridge. @@ /_images/518ab92f8e42d88b.jpg]\n10:51 am\n- \n[IMG A toddler enjoys the playroom at the Cranmore Children's Hospital. @@ /_images/ada5a7bf1f6e2e2d.jpg]\n10:45 am\n- \n[IMG A professor of applied physics, electrical engineering and computer science, holds a chariot posture in his office on North Ridge. @@ /_images/51f64b7f00b7c5b0.jpg]\n10:26 am\n- \n[IMG A research scientist at the Corravale Herbarium. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n11:12 am\n- \n[IMG Psychology Commencement 2019 @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n11:38 am\n- \n[IMG A student from the Center for Sustainable Systems wearing a gray shirt and denim jacket points to a QR code at the bottom of a poster with information about the group while talking with an attendee at EarthFest 2024. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n11:03 am\n- \n[IMG In a Chemistry Department lab, a student examines a set of nanoscale imaging agents created for use in drug and gene delivery. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n11:47 am\n- \n[IMG Students test a prosthetic foot in the Human Biomechanics and Motion Lab. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n12:05 pm\n- \n[IMG Looking up at Vantage Memorial Tower through spring flowers. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n12:41 pm\n- \n[IMG ROTC cadets and adaptive sports athletes from two rival universities make their way down one of the sidewalks near the central green in the final leg of the Great State Race, carrying the game balls between the two campus towns in support of campus disability services offices. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n12:33 pm\n- \n[IMG A music student uses the natural acoustics of the woods to practice his french horn on North Ridge. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n12:19 pm\n- \n[IMG Visitors view staff artwork in the Building 18 Rotunda Gallery at the North Ridge Research Center. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n12:52 pm\n- \n[IMG Students on the sidewalk under the Central Campus Transit Center awning hurriedly step off and board a sleek electric-blue bus bound for the North Ridge dorms. The arrival boards hanging above the crowd of students on the sidewalk display the bus schedule. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n1:15 pm\n- \n[IMG A research team in the Ideation Lab develops a sensor ring that collects a patient's vital health data on campus. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n2:07 pm\n- \n[IMG A research team in the Ideation Lab develops a sensor ring that gathers a patient's vital health data on campus. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n2:44 pm\n- \n[IMG The Movement Science 437 class outfits a student in a motion-detection sensor suit for a study on how knee injuries limit motion. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n2:26 pm\n- \n[IMG A view of the School of Public Health seen through the tunnel. @@ /_images/placeholder_152.svg]\n2:58 pm\n<div class=\"clear\" \n########## parents ##########\nid=\"content\" role=\"main\">\n## Parents\nP: Welcome to the Corravale family. Sending a student to college is a milestone for every household. Corravale is dedicated to helping parents and students make the most of this chapter by sharing up-to-date information about campus life, key dates, and upcoming events.\n#### For Parents & Families\n- [L /_404.html] C-Parent\n- [L /_404.html] Undergraduate Admissions\n- [L /_404.html] Portal en Espanol\n#### Health & Safety\n- [L /_404.html] University Health & Counseling\n- [L /_404.html] Counseling & Psychological Services\n- [L /_404.html] Public Safety and Security\n#### Tools & Resources\n- [L /_404.html] Academic Schedule\n- [L /_404.html] Social Media Listings\n- [L /_404.html] Campus Visit Details\n- [L /_404.html] Parent & Family Support\n#### News & Updates\n- [L /_404.html] Corravale DailyCampus Newspaper\n- [L /_404.html] Corravale News\n- [L /_404.html] Campus Calendar\n- [L /_404.html] Top Topics\n#### Tuition & Aid Details\n- [L /_404.html] Costs for In-State Students\n- [L /_404.html] Fees & Tuition\n- [L /_404.html] Aid & Gr